        "id": 1076123
      },
      "writtenOn": "2021-02-10T22:33:06Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "So the bits specify which channels are included, but their order is constant.  i.e., front left will always come before front right, if they are both included.\n\nI feel like the ordering is a separate issue.  Maybe we could just split the sentence.\n\nThis is also a bitfield, which specifies which channels are included in the outgoing media packet.  The data in the packet has the same order as the bitfield (i.e., the data enabled by bit 2 comes before the data enabled by bit 3).",
      "parentUuid": "2a19c59f_6d6ca166",
